    "cost_closing_html":  "Sirloin instead of a pricier steak keeps this affordable, and the pico and guac are just produce. Catch the beef on sale and the cost tab number falls with it.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSirloin is the smart carne asada cut.\u003c/strong\u003e It grills fast, slices thin against the grain, and costs far less than the cuts the restaurants use. Buy it on sale and freeze extra.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy the avocados a little firm.\u003c/strong\u003e Grab them a few days ahead and let them ripen on the counter so they are perfect on prep day and you are not paying for pre-made guac.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePico is cheap produce and a knife.\u003c/strong\u003e A tomato, a bit of red onion, a jalapeno, cilantro, and lime make more pico than a plastic tub for a fraction of the price."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice per the package and set it aside.",
                    "Toss the sliced sirloin with the minced garlic, the cumin, the chili powder, the salt, and half of the lime juice, then sear it hard in a hot dry pan until the edges char. Rest it and slice thin against the grain.",
                    "Drain and rinse the black beans and warm them through.",
                    "Make the pico: dice the tomato, red onion, and jalapeno, chop the cilantro, and toss with the rest of the lime juice and a pinch of salt.",
                    "Mash the avocado into a quick guacamole with a little of the pico and a squeeze of lime.",
                    "Warm the tortillas, then portion and wrap as below, layering rice, beans, steak, guacamole, and pico."
                ],
